      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Legal sources for educational video</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">TED Talks, Khan Academy, MIT OpenCourseWare, Crash Course, and many university channels publish content under Creative Commons or educational licenses. Some platforms include a download button directly on the video page. When a download button is available, use it first.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Step-by-step guide</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Find the educational video on a trusted platform.</li><li>Check if the video has a download button or Creative Commons license.</li><li>If no direct download is available, copy the public URL.</li><li>Paste the URL into a downloader like ClipVault.</li><li>Choose MP4 or MP3 and save the file for personal study.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Helpful tips</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
